 "id": "y11-8-1-arith",
 "label": "8.1 L3: Arithmetic Operators",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "do-now",
   "label": "Do Now: Data Types (1 of 2)",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y11ar-do-now",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Data Types (1 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why are there quote marks around M?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>They show it is text, not a number or a variable.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From 8.1 L2. Cambridge IGCSE 0478/23, November 2025, Question 3.</p><div id=\"y11ar-do-now\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Tick one box to identify the most appropriate data type to store 'M'",
     "options": [
      "integer",
      "char",
      "real",
      "Boolean"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "'M' is one character in quote marks."
    }
   ],
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: choose a data type",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "We will find the best data type for <strong>4.5</strong>. Your question has a different value, so you still do the working yourself.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">4.5</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Ask: is it only TRUE or FALSE? <strong>No.</strong> So it is not Boolean.",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr class=\"wt-hl\"><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>No</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does it have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr></table>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Ask: is it a number? <strong>Yes.</strong> 4.5 is a number. It is not in quote marks.",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>No</strong></td></tr><tr class=\"wt-hl\"><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>Yes</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does it have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr></table>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Ask: does it have a decimal point? <strong>Yes</strong>: 4<span class=\"wt-hl\">.</span>5",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>No</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>Yes</strong></td></tr><tr class=\"wt-hl\"><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does it have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>Yes</strong></td></tr></table>"
     },
     {
      "text": "A number with a decimal point is <strong>real</strong>. Integer stores whole numbers only, so it cannot store 4.5.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">4.5 &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">real</span></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Now ask the same questions about the value in your question. Look at the quote marks too: they mean text.",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does it have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr></table>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Declare Variables (2 of 2)",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11ar-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y11ar_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Declare Variables (2 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why must every variable be declared first?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>The program must know its name and what kind of value it stores before it can use it.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From 8.1 L1 and L2. Cambridge IGCSE 0478/23, November 2025, Question 9(a). Name holds the name of a person. Age holds the age of a person as a whole number. Found holds a flag that can be set to TRUE or FALSE. Write pseudocode statements to declare the variables Name, Age and Found.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y11ar-do-now-2-a\">(a) Declare Name [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Declare Variables (2 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y11ar-do-now-2-b\">(b) Declare Age [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-do-now-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Declare Variables (2 of 2) part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y11ar-do-now-2-c\">(c) Declare Found [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-do-now-2-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-c\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Declare Variables (2 of 2) part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ar-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11ar-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>",
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: declare variables",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "A similar question: <strong>Height</strong> holds a height in metres, such as 1.65. <strong>Grade</strong> holds one letter, such as 'B'.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">Height: 1.65 &nbsp;&nbsp; Grade: 'B'</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Every line starts with the keyword <strong>DECLARE</strong>.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line wt-hl\">DECLARE</div></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Then the variable's name, then a <strong>colon</strong>.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line wt-hl\">DECLARE Height :</div></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "1.65 is a number with a decimal point. So the type is <strong>REAL</strong>.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line wt-hl\">DECLARE Height : REAL</div></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "'B' is one character. So the type is <strong>CHAR</strong>. One line for each variable.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Height : REAL</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line wt-hl\">DECLARE Grade : CHAR</div></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Check each line: DECLARE, the name, a colon, the type. Now do the same for Name, Age and Found.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line wt-hl\">DECLARE Height : REAL</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line wt-hl\">DECLARE Grade : CHAR</div></div>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-ext",
   "label": "Extension: Do Now Challenge",
   "type": "embedded-app",
