   "embedContainerId": "y11ar-do-now-ext",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: Do Now Challenge</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\"><strong>Extension:</strong> finished the Do Now? Try these questions from 8.1 L1 and L2: variables, constants, data types, INPUT and OUTPUT. Stuck? Switch on <strong>I need help</strong> to see a similar question worked through.</p><div id=\"y11ar-do-now-ext\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "title",
   "label": "Arithmetic Operators",
   "content": "<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">8.1 Programming Concepts</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Arithmetic Operators</h2><p>Year 11</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Today:</strong> an <strong>operator</strong> is a symbol that does maths with values.</li><li><strong>Then:</strong> DIV and MOD: dividing into whole groups, and what is left over.</li><li><strong>Activities:</strong> trace a program, then write lines and run them.</li></ul><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does a program need to do maths?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>To work out totals, prices, scores and times from the values it stores.</p></div></details>"
  },
  {
   "id": "operators",
   "label": "Five Arithmetic Operators",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Five Arithmetic Operators</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: what is 7 / 2? What is 7 ^ 2?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>7 / 2 = <strong>3.5</strong>. / gives a number with a decimal point when it does not divide exactly.</p><p>7 ^ 2 = 7 * 7 = <strong>49</strong>.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Operator</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">It means</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Example</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>+</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">add</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 + 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>-</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">subtract</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 - 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>*</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">multiply</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 * 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>/</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">divide</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 / 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>^</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">raised to the power of</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 ^ 2</td></tr></table><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>In a program: <code>Area &lt;- Length * Width</code></li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "check-ops",
   "label": "Check: Use the Operators",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11ar-check-ops",
   "validatorKey": "y11ar_check_ops",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Use the Operators</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is 3 ^ 2 not 6?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>3 ^ 2 is 3 * 3. 6 is 3 * 2, a different operator.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Work out each one.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-ops-a\">(a) What is 6 * 4? [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-ops-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-ops-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Use the Operators part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-ops-b\">(b) What is 9 / 2? [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-ops-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-ops-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Use the Operators part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-ops-c\">(c) What is 3 ^ 2? [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-ops-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-ops-c\" aria-label=\"Check: Use the Operators part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-ops-d\">(d) Write the operator that means raised to the power of. [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-ops-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-ops-d\" aria-label=\"Check: Use the Operators part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ar-check-ops-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11ar-check-ops-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "div-mod",
   "label": "DIV and MOD",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">DIV and MOD</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: 17 sweets go into bags of 5. How many full bags? How many sweets are left over?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p><strong>3</strong> full bags, so DIV(17, 5) returns 3.</p><p><strong>2</strong> sweets left over, so MOD(17, 5) returns 2.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">17 sweets, bags of 5</p><div style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid var(--muted, #999);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 6px;margin:4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid var(--muted, #999);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 6px;margin:4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid var(--muted, #999);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 6px;margin:4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span></span><br><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent, #6aa9ff);margin:2px\"></span></div></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>DIV(17, 5)</strong>: how many <strong>full groups</strong> of 5?</li><li>DIV gives the <strong>quotient</strong>: the whole number part. The <strong>fractional part</strong> is thrown away.</li><li><strong>MOD(17, 5)</strong>: how many are <strong>left over</strong>?</li><li>MOD gives the <strong>remainder</strong>.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "compare",
   "label": "Compare: /, DIV and MOD",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: /, DIV and MOD</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Look at each row. What is the same about / and DIV? When does MOD give 0?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>DIV is the / answer with the fractional part thrown away.</p><p>MOD gives 0 when the numbers divide exactly: 20 bags of 5, nothing left.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Numbers</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">/ divide</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">DIV quotient</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">MOD remainder</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">17 and 5</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">17 / 5 = 3.4</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">DIV(17, 5) = 3</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">MOD(17, 5) = 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">20 and 5</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">20 / 5 = 4</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">DIV(20, 5) = 4</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">MOD(20, 5) = 0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 and 2</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">7 / 2 = 3.5</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">DIV(7, 2) = 3</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">MOD(7, 2) = 1</td></tr></table><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Exam papers also write <strong>17 DIV 5</strong> and <strong>17 MOD 5</strong>. They mean the same as DIV(17, 5) and MOD(17, 5).</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "check-divmod",
   "label": "Check: DIV and MOD",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11ar-check-divmod",
   "validatorKey": "y11ar_check_divmod",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: DIV and MOD</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is MOD(12, 4) a useful check?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It tells you if 4 goes into 12 exactly: the remainder is 0.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Work out each one.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-divmod-a\">(a) DIV(23, 5) [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-divmod-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-divmod-a\" aria-label=\"Check: DIV and MOD part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-divmod-b\">(b) MOD(23, 5) [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-divmod-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-divmod-b\" aria-label=\"Check: DIV and MOD part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-divmod-c\">(c) MOD(12, 4) [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-divmod-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-divmod-c\" aria-label=\"Check: DIV and MOD part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-check-divmod-d\">(d) DIV(9, 2) [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-check-divmod-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-divmod-d\" aria-label=\"Check: DIV and MOD part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ar-check-divmod-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11ar-check-divmod-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-355",
   "label": "Exam Question: DIV, / and MOD",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11ar-exam-355",
   "validatorKey": "y11ar_exam_355",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: DIV, / and MOD</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">355 DIV 10 is written without brackets. Does it mean something different?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>No. 355 DIV 10 means the same as DIV(355, 10).</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/23, June 2025, Question 2. Three uses of arithmetic operators are shown. Write the correct result for each. Use one of: 5, 355, 35, 35.5 (one is not used).</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-exam-355-a\">(a) 355 DIV 10 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-exam-355-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-355-a\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: DIV, / and MOD part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-exam-355-b\">(b) 355 / 10 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-exam-355-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-355-b\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: DIV, / and MOD part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ar-exam-355-c\">(c) 355 MOD 10 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ar-exam-355-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-355-c\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: DIV, / and MOD part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ar-exam-355-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11ar-exam-355-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
